From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] agent: deliver STA notifications during onboarding

A OneWifi association can arrive as soon as an M2-created BSS becomes active,
while the corresponding EasyMesh radio is still completing AP capability or
topology synchronization.  sta_list orchestration currently waits for the
radio to reach configured/topo_synchronized and expires after ten seconds.
The association remains live in OneWifi, but its one-shot Client Association
Event never reaches the controller.

Topology notifications are fire-and-forget and do not own a response
transaction.  Allow sta_list to execute in any radio state, send its snapshot
synchronously, preserve the radio's prior onboarding state, and mark the
orchestration complete.  This also removes the next-protocol-tick window in
which another exchange could overwrite agent_topology_notify before it sends.

---
 src/em/em.cpp                 | 12 +++++++++++-
 src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp    |  9 +++++----
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/em/em.cpp b/src/em/em.cpp
--- a/src/em/em.cpp
+++ b/src/em/em.cpp
@@ -93,9 +93,19 @@ void em_t::orch_execute(em_cmd_t *pcmd)
     // now set the em state to start message exchages with peer
     cmd_type = pcmd->m_type;
     switch (cmd_type) {
-        case em_cmd_type_sta_list:
+        case em_cmd_type_sta_list: {
+            /* Client Association Event notifications are fire-and-forget and
+             * carry no response transaction.  Send this command snapshot in
+             * the orchestrator call itself.  Preserve any onboarding state
+             * (for example ap_cap_report) rather than using the shared radio
+             * state machine as temporary notification storage. */
+            em_state_t saved_state = m_sm.get_state();
             m_sm.set_state(em_state_agent_topology_notify);
+            em_configuration_t::process_agent_state();
+            m_sm.set_state(saved_state);
+            m_orch_state = em_orch_state_fini;
 			break;
+        }
 
         case em_cmd_type_set_ssid:
         case em_cmd_type_set_radio:
diff --git a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
--- a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
@@ -176,10 +176,11 @@ bool em_orch_agent_t::is_em_ready_for_orch_exec(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em)
 			return true;
 		}
     } else if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_sta_list) {
-		if ((em->get_state() == em_state_agent_configured) ||
-				(em->get_state() >= em_state_agent_topo_synchronized)){
-			return true;
-		}
+		/* A live OneWifi association can arrive while this radio is finishing
+		 * onboarding (commonly ap_cap_report).  The notification sender does
+		 * not require a response and orch_execute() preserves that state, so
+		 * delaying here only lets the one-shot command expire after 10 seconds. */
+		return true;
     } else if (pcmd->m_type == em_cmd_type_sta_link_metrics) {
 		if (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_configured) {
 			return true;
